    <heading level="1">13.2. Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The figure shows a curve $$C$$ given by a vector function $$\mathbf{r}{(t)}$$ .</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Draw the vectors $$\mathbf{r}{(4.5)} - \mathbf{r}{(4)}$$ and $$\mathbf{r}{(4.2)} - \mathbf{r}{(4)}$$ .</item>
          <item>Draw the vectors $$\frac{\mathbf{r}{(4.5)} - \mathbf{r}{(4)}}{0.5}$$ and $$\frac{\mathbf{r}{(4.2)} - \mathbf{r}{(4)}}{0.2}$$</item>
          <item>Write expressions for $$\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(4)}$$ and the unit tangent vector $$\mathbf{T}{(4)}$$ .</item>
          <item>Draw the vector $$\mathbf{T}{(4)}$$ . Details A curve and three vectors are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. Both the axes have a single tick mark labeled 1. The curve, labeled C, resembles a part of a cardioid with its cusp opening downward. It begins from the origin, goes down to the right, then goes up to the right, crosses the x axis at approximately (0.75, 0), goes upward bulging to the right, and passes through points P, Q, and R as it ascends. The three vectors begin from the origin and slope upward to the right to meet the curve. The first vector is labeled vector r(4), slopes gradually upward to the right, and meets the curve at P. The second vector is labeled vector r(4, 2), slopes upward to the right, and meets the curve at Q located up and to the right of P. The third vector is labeled vector r(4, 5), slopes steeply upward to the right, and meets the curve at R located up and to the left of P.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(4)} = \lim\limits_{h\rightarrow 0}\frac{\mathbf{r}{({4 + h})} - \mathbf{r}{(4)}}{h}$$ ; $$\mathbf{T}{(4)} = \frac{\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(4)}}{\left| {\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(4)}} \right|}$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
