          <item>Draw the vector $$\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(1)}$$ starting at $$(1,1)$$ , and compare it with the vector $$\frac{\mathbf{r}{(1.1)} - \mathbf{r}{(1)}}{0.1}$$ Explain why these vectors are so close to each other in length and direction.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <instruction>3, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8 Sketch the plane curve with the given vector equation. Find $$\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(t)}$$ . Sketch the position vector $$\mathbf{r}{(t)}$$ and the tangent vector $$\mathbf{r}^{\prime}{(t)}$$ for the given value of $$t$$ .</instruction>
